  "reflectionQuestion": "Have you ever had to keep asking for something even when everything around you said to be quiet?",
  "reflectionText": "He had sat by that road for years. When he heard Jesus passing, he shouted. When people told him to be quiet, he shouted louder. Jesus stopped and asked what he wanted. The answer was simple and direct — not a negotiation, just the thing itself: that I might see. What is it to believe that a voice from the roadside is not too small to be heard at all?",
